      "assistant_text": "According to [[write-journal]], the Guarded Write Journal describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**.\n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state (its previous content if it existed, or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist) into an in-memory write journal.\n- If an agent run fails\u2014due to a turn cap being exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or all writes being denied\u2014the journal can roll every recorded write back in reverse order.\n- This rollback restores previous content for files that existed and deletes files that were newly created.\n- The journal provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without needing a database transaction\u2014the journal itself acts as the transaction log, held in memory for the duration of one run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses this journal\u0027s rollback capability, since it has no write tool at all.",
